        "denialFound": "Found in the same source, and the record already holds it as c042. The Wire (PTI), https://thewire.in/business/uk-court-orders-anil-ambani-to-pay-717-million-to-chinese-banks-within-21-days: \"ICBC ... made their claim based on an alleged guarantee that was never signed by Ambani and he has consistently denied having authorised anyone to execute any guarantee on his behalf\"; \"It is emphasised that it is not a personal loan of Ambani\"; the amount will \"reduce substantially\" once RCom's insolvency is resolved; \"the question of any enforcement in India does not arise in the near future\". The spokesperson was asked for comment. I did not look for later reports of an appeal because the web-search budget was used up. The record's killIf says none was reported.",
        "innocentReading": "The ruling holds regardless of any charitable reading. The only non-damning context is Ambani's own position: the loan was a corporate loan to RCom, he says he never signed or authorised the guarantee, and the final amount is to be \"assessed subject to the outcome of the RCom Insolvency Action\", so the $716.9m may come down. The claim wording should keep that point and should not describe the money as a personal loan.",
        "reason": "I opened the source and pulled the full article text from the page's structured data (JSON-LD). It supports every figure in the claim: \"the sum payable by the Defendant to the Claimant (banks) pursuant to the Guarantee is $716,917,681.51\"; \"It is declared that the Guarantee is binding on the Defendant\"; Justice Nigel Teare; the three named banks; principal $549,804,650.16 + interest $51,923,451.49 + default interest $115,189,579.86; £750,000 costs; a 21-day deadline; and the RCom 2012 refinancing. The judge, date, currency, parties and direction of the edge are all correct, and the denial is recorded in c042. \"Reported\" is the right tier: this is one outlet carrying PTI wire copy that quotes the court order directly, and I did not obtain the order itself or a second independent outlet. The rupee figure is our own conversion and does not appear in the source. That makes it a precision issue, not grounds to refute.",
