        "reason": "The quantitative core holds against the cited primary source. I re-summed the PDF's \"List of Awarded Completed Contracts\": 19 packages, US$1,223.82m. L&T (P3 243.10 + P7 98.57 + P17 88.37) = 430.04 (35.1%). Afcons (P6 144.69 + P8 208.38) = 353.07 (28.9%). STEC P4 153.57 (12.5%). Ircon P19 98.50 (8.0%). L&T plus Afcons = 63.99%. It is correctly labelled \"estimated value\" and correctly tiered analytic, being our own arithmetic on a documented plan with no wrongdoing implied. The source check is only partial for two reasons. First, \"Package 4 drew five bidders\" is not in the cited ADB PDF. It is confirmed by Urban Transport News (2020-06-12), which the file lists but the claim's srcs does not. Second, \"₹1,000 cr+ viaduct/tunnel packages\" overstates the case: at ₹73.5/US$, P7 (≈₹725 cr), P17 (≈₹650 cr) and P19 (≈₹724 cr) are under ₹1,000 cr, and P17 and P19 are trackwork and traction, not viaduct or tunnel. Neither defect breaks the claim, so it survives as analytic with corrections.",
