        "denialFound": "No denial found. He was asked and did not answer. ThePrint, Moushumi Das Gupta, 2025-05-05 (https://theprint.in/india/krishnamurthy-subramanian-had-6-months-still-left-in-his-tenure-at-imf-why-did-modi-govt-recall-him/2615392/): \"Subramanian was not available for comment despite repeated attempts to contact him on his mobile phone.\" The same article: \"Government sources said, following the curtailment of his service, Subramanian resigned from his post citing personal reasons.\" That is second-hand, from government sources, not his own statement. Neither Business Standard source (2025-05-03, 2025-05-05) mentions asking him. The 2025-05-05 piece records only that the IMF spokesperson answered by email and that \"The Ministry of Finance did not respond to a query on the matter.\" The PTI piece on the Union Bank book purchase (ThePrint, 2025-05-06) carries no comment from Subramanian.",
        "innocentReading": "He stayed quiet on unofficial, source-based allegations while an ACC decision was fresh and while the Union Bank procurement review and an ISB review (Mint/Moneycontrol, 15 May 2025) were under way. Silence at that point is routine and consistent with innocence. It is not evidence for or against the book-promotion or IMF-dataset explanations.",
        "reason": "The decisive problem is the claim's wording, \"asked/not asked unknown\". That is false: ThePrint (5 May 2025) says reporters tried repeatedly to reach him by mobile phone and he was not available for comment. So the record says \"asked, no response\", with one named credible outlet as the source. The claim also has an empty srcs array, and neither cited Business Standard article says anything about approaching him. The edge as written is therefore unsourced and factually wrong about whether he was asked. The underlying finding, that no response from him is on record, survives, but at the tier of one credible outlet: reported. \"Alleged\" is the tier for the accusation in c020. It is the wrong tier for a documented non-response.",
