          "1. Claim text: delete \"since a lower 2014 base mechanically compounds faster\". Replace with: \"6 of 7 peer EMs (BRA, IDN, MEX, TUR, ZAF, THA; not PHL) show the same 2004-14 to 2014-24 deceleration in World Bank DT.DOD.DECT.CD, so the gap is not partisan-discriminating. Ext. debt/GDP was 17.4% (2004), 22.4% (2014) and 19.1% (2024).\"\n2. innocentReading: remove the base-effect sentence and the claim that the taper tantrum raises the UPA figure. Replace with the global cycle, slower US$ GDP growth (11.1% vs 6.3%), the post-2014 dollar/rupee valuation shrinking rupee-denominated liabilities, and the private ECB/NRI share.\n3. Target node: change \"t\" from min:ministry-of-finance to a total-external-debt / India-economy node. Otherwise restrict the claim to PPG (DT.DOD.DPPG.CD: $64.9bn, $152.5bn, $238.9bn; about 8.9% vs 4.6% CAGR).\n4. symmetryCheck narrative: apply the same fix. Remove the \"3.7x-larger base mechanically produces a lower percentage growth rate\" wording.\n5. Note in \"d\" that the calendar-year cut places 2014 partly in NDA tenure; the alternative 2004-13 / 2014-23 cut gives 14.8% / 3.9%.\n6. killIf values: PPG was $205.3bn in 2021 and $214.9bn in 2023, which is consistent as stated."
