        "innocentReading": "An ADB-financed open competitive tender (international advertisement, all ADB member countries eligible) was already past technical and financial evaluation before the clash and the July 2020 Order. Five bidders, all qualified; STEC was L1 by ₹44 cr (3.8%) under L&T. Chinese firms had routinely won MDB-funded Indian packages under both UPA and NDA. Cancelling would have meant re-tendering, a higher price, delay, and possible friction with ADB and its co-financiers AIIB/NDB. Counter-weight the status line omits: the Order's own text ('If this stage has been crossed, ordinarily the tenders will be cancelled and the process started de novo'), plus the ADB PP's 'Except as ADB may otherwise agree', show there was discretion. So 'undercut' is too strong; 'contested' is right.",
