        "innocentReading": "DEA clears state external-aid proposals against a fiscal and priority screen, and the lender's own pipeline adds more filtering. That screen applies to every state: the 3%-of-GSDP ceiling, whether the state can repay, and the state's past record of using up its borrowing limit. Kerala's constraint in FY2023-24 came from its own admitted over-borrowing in FY2017-18 to FY2019-20 plus off-budget liabilities counted within the ceiling, not from its party. Meanwhile the same Union posed a US$250m IDA-blend DPO for Kerala in 2019, and it posed dozens of World Bank, ADB and AIIB operations for DMK/AIADMK Tamil Nadu, TMC West Bengal, Congress/AAP Punjab and Congress Karnataka. Per-capita differences are driven mostly by small hill and north-eastern states and by project pipeline timing, under both UPA and NDA.",
